MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The powered USB hub and full-size mouse fit my recent effort to make my laptop workspace more useful, alongside my keyboard, networking cables and desk accessories.",
    "The microSD card and flash drive offer practical ways to try another Raspberry Pi setup and move files between devices, which fits my history of buying storage and connection accessories."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The streaming stick and tablet add devices without addressing a need I have right now; owning a Kindle and Raspberry Pi does not mean I want another screen or streaming device.",
    "More wired earbuds feel redundant because I already have headphones and a headset, while the internal hard drive and laptop RAM require an upgrade plan and compatibility checks I have not established."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been stretched into interest in almost any electronic device, even when it serves a different purpose from my recent purchases.",
    "Buying an accessory before seems to be treated as a reason to buy another similar one, without enough attention to whether it adds a useful capability or repeats something I already have."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent cable, Ethernet adapter, headphone mount and cleaning purchases point toward connecting, organizing and maintaining my existing workspace.",
    "The specific benefit matters: a spare microSD card lets me keep separate Raspberry Pi setups, and a powered USB 3.0 hub is more useful to me here than a second, slower hub."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in practical computer accessories but stretched it too far into extra devices and unplanned upgrades."
}
